 "text": "Hello! How's everything today? It' not random, there's a pattern. Think about it, there are two sets of them, one ends in an e and the other doesn't. Let me double-check, but I' fairly sure about it. So, the first one you learn is usually the one that ends in e, like man or mann. It' not silly, it' the way our brains learn. Then you learn the other set the same way, starting with the one that doesn't end in e. Probably, and that's why it's so easy to remember. Now try matching them to the right pronouns. He, she, it, they.",
